# Module-wide options, all BEACON_*.

menu "Beacon"

config BEACON_BACKLIGHT_BRIGHTNESS
    int "Backlight brightness of the lit screen (percent)"
    range 0 100
    default 80
    depends on LED_PWM
    help
      Duty cycle written to the pwm-leds backlight before the display driver
      starts. The unit has no ambient light sensor, so a lit screen keeps
      this value; BEACON_SCREEN_OFF_AFTER_S turns the backlight off and back
      on to it.

config BEACON_SCREEN_OFF_AFTER_S
    int "Turn the screen off after this many seconds without a key press (0 = never)"
    range 0 86400
    default 300
    depends on SHIELD_PROSPECTOR && ZMK_DISPLAY_STATUS_SCREEN_CUSTOM && LED_PWM
    help
      Once the keyboard's status payload has counted no key press for this
      long, the backlight fades out within a second and the panel is
      blanked; the next key press lights the screen again (src/screen_off.c).
      Only the keyboard's key presses count, any key of either half: the
      device hears nothing else, so a pointing device does not keep the
      screen lit. Until the first key press the time since boot counts, so
      the screen also goes dark when no keyboard is heard. 0: the screen
      stays lit.

config BEACON_SCREEN_OFF
    bool
    default y if BEACON_SCREEN_OFF_AFTER_S > 0
    help
      Set when BEACON_SCREEN_OFF_AFTER_S is above 0.

config BEACON_BOOTLOADER_ON_1200_BAUD
    bool "Enter the UF2 bootloader on a 1200 baud touch"
    depends on USB_CDC_ACM
    select RETENTION_BOOT_MODE
    select CDC_ACM_DTE_RATE_CALLBACK_SUPPORT
    help
      When the host sets any CDC ACM port of the device to 1200 baud (for
      example "stty -f /dev/cu.usbmodemXXXX 1200" on macOS), set the retained
      boot mode to bootloader and warm-reboot 250 ms later, so the UF2
      bootloader mounts its drive without a reset double-tap. The delay lets
      the host's control transfer complete before the device resets.

      Any program that sets the port to 1200 baud, a serial monitor included,
      reboots the device. The prospector shield turns this on by default
      because the unit has no key for &bootloader and no touch input.

      The boot mode needs the board's retention support (RETENTION, a
      zephyr,boot-mode retention area; ZMK's xiao_ble board has both). It is
      selected rather than depended on, so a board without it fails the
      Kconfig step instead of silently building without the entry.

config BEACON_SCREEN_DUMP
    bool "Send the screen to the host on a 2400 baud touch"
    depends on BEACON_BOOTLOADER_ON_1200_BAUD && ZMK_DISPLAY && LV_COLOR_DEPTH_16
    select UART_INTERRUPT_DRIVEN
    select CRC
    help
      When the host sets the CDC ACM port to 2400 baud, render the whole
      screen once more and send it over that port as RGB565 bands closed by
      a CRC-32 (the format: src/screen_dump.c), which canon's
      "scripts/dongle.py shot" turns into a PNG. The screen stands still
      while the bands go out, and a logging image drops the log lines of
      that time: the dump has the port to itself.

      It uses the 1200 baud entry's rate callback (the CDC ACM class driver
      keeps one per device), hence the dependency. The prospector shield
      turns this on by default.

config BEACON_SPRITE_GIF
    string "GIF sprite embedded in the image (absolute path, empty = none)"
    default ""
    depends on SHIELD_PROSPECTOR && ZMK_DISPLAY_STATUS_SCREEN_CUSTOM
    help
      Absolute path of a GIF89a file with a global colour table (the only
      kind LVGL's gifdec opens). The build embeds its bytes in the image and
      the status screen plays it above the HP bar, scaled to fill the space
      between the panel's top edge and the bar: at SPEED_PCT of its own tempo
      (src/sprite.c) while nobody types, and stepped by the key presses the
      keyboard's broadcaster counts
      while it is typed on (src/sprite.c). Empty: no sprite, which is what CI
      and the release build.

      The build fails when the GIF does not fit that space at 1x
      (src/prospector_screen.c), or when its decoder's share of the LVGL
      pool, kept for the whole run, does not fit CONFIG_LV_Z_MEM_POOL_SIZE
      next to the screen (CMakeLists.txt; the prospector shield's default
      grows with a sprite). Local builds: scripts/build.sh --sprite <gif>
      [--sprite-name <text>].

config BEACON_SPRITE
    bool
    default y if BEACON_SPRITE_GIF != ""
    select LV_USE_IMAGE
    select LV_USE_GIF
    select LV_GIF_CACHE_DECODE_DATA
    select SYS_HEAP_RUNTIME_STATS if LOG
    help
      Set when BEACON_SPRITE_GIF names a file. LV_GIF_CACHE_DECODE_DATA is a
      correctness requirement here, not a speed option (src/sprite.c).
      LV_USE_IMAGE only lets LVGL's lv_gif.c, which LV_USE_GIF compiles,
      build: the sprite draws itself. With logging on, the sprite's minute
      line reports the LVGL pool's allocated and peak bytes, the numbers the
      pool size is chosen from.

config BEACON_SPRITE_NAME
    string "Name of the sprite, shown under the HP bar (empty = none)"
    default ""
    help
      The name is a second row of the HP bar's box, at the left in unscii
      16: the box grows by that row and the sprite's space above it shrinks
      (src/hp_bar.h). 15 glyphs fit; a longer name is cut. Printable ASCII
      only: the font has no other glyphs, a double quote or a backslash would
      need Kconfig escaping, and "??" would be a C trigraph in autoconf.h.
      Empty: no second row, the screen of CI and the release build, which
      have no sprite. The HP bar shows the name only with a sprite
      (src/hp_bar.h).

      No dependency on purpose: kconfig.py prints the value of any assigned
      symbol whose value did not take, so a dependency on BEACON_SPRITE
      would print the name in every build where the sprite ends up off (a
      display-off --kconfig, another shield).

      Like the GIF, the name is a personal file's and never goes into a
      repository: a local build passes it (scripts/build.sh --sprite <gif>
      --sprite-name <text>, through a Kconfig fragment so that a failed
      configure step, whose command line west prints, shows only the
      fragment's path; canon derives it from the GIF's file name with its
      assets/sprite-name.sh).

config BEACON_STATUS_BROADCAST
    bool "Broadcast the keyboard's status on a second advertising set"
    depends on ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL && BT && SETTINGS
    select BT_EXT_ADV
    help
      On the keyboard's split central, advertise the status payload (each
      half's battery, the highest active layer and its name, and a count of
      key presses; src/status_payload.h) as manufacturer data in a legacy,
      non-connectable, non-scannable advertising set next to ZMK's own
      connectable one, refreshed every BEACON_PAYLOAD_INTERVAL_MS
      (src/status_payload.h) and right after a key press. The Prospector
      Dongle's observer (the prospector shield) reads it.

      The consumer's config must also set CONFIG_BT_EXT_ADV_MAX_ADV_SET=2:
      with BT_EXT_ADV the host takes ZMK's legacy advertising from the same
      pool of sets, and the build fails on a pool of 1. BT_EXT_ADV costs
      about 34 KB of flash and 11 KB of RAM on nRF52840 and switches the host
      to the extended HCI commands.

endmenu
